# Files Prettier must never touch.
#
# GENERATED. `just check` compares each of these byte-for-byte against a fresh
# regeneration. Formatting one makes that gate fail permanently: the generator
# emits its own layout, so the committed file would differ from the regenerated
# one on every run and the only repair is to un-format it. Add a generated file
# here the same day you add its generator.

# Generated from the Catalogue by `just client`; gated by _check-client-fresh.
src/lib/api/catalogue.ts

# Generated by `just css` from the design tokens; gated by _check-tokens-fresh.
static/manifest.webmanifest

# Compiled from messages/ by inlang paraglide on every build. Gitignored, and it
# ships its own .prettierignore saying the same thing.
src/lib/paraglide/

# The design tokens. Not generated — hand-written, and the source `just css`
# compiles into the committed assets/app.css. Prettier's tab indentation does
# not stay in this file: Tailwind passes it through into selector lists and
# unicode-range values of the compiled stylesheet, so formatting here puts
# literal tabs mid-line in the artefact that actually ships, and breaks
# _check-tokens-fresh until assets/app.css is regenerated to match. The comment
# columns are also aligned by hand on purpose (issue #80). Left alone on both
# counts — it is one file, and it is already consistent.
src/app.css

# OWNED BY ANOTHER TOOL. Nothing is gated on these, but each is rewritten by
# something that has its own opinion about layout, so formatting them starts a
# fight that repeats on every write and settles nothing.

# npm rewrites both on every install, and the lockfile is machine-authored.
package.json
package-lock.json

# The translation catalogues and inlang's own settings. These are data, sorted
# and written by the inlang tooling — not source to be laid out. Paraglide's
# config beside them is hand-written source, and formatted like any other.
messages/
project.inlang/*
!project.inlang/paraglide.config.js

# Build output — none of it is committed.
build/
.svelte-kit/
node_modules/
